"welfare_kg":3000.0,"binding":"do","yield":143.6},{"t_c":22.0,"do_kg":239.4,"nh3_kg":16545.1,"welfare_kg":3000.0,"binding":"do","yield":0.0}],"bio_settings":{"salinity_psu":30,"ph":7.6,"flow_m3_h":400,"tank_m3":100,"species":"generic salmonid (PLACEHOLDER)","t_opt":15.0,"t_max":22.0,"placeholder":true},"ceiling_c":12.25,"ceiling_binding":"do"},"reported":{"source":"Findings reported from the Colab runs of the rebuilt notebooks (not recomputed on this page).","thermal":[{"title":"Per-port asymptote bug","text":"The near-field cell used total diffuser flow where the law needs per-port flow. Two algebraic forms of the same law disagreed by 84% while the cell printed that the constants agreed. Fixed; the library now enforces per-port and per-length fluxes."},{"title":"Domain narrower than the tide","text":"About 26% of the heat was being lost because the plume advected out of a domain narrower than the tidal excursion (about 10.7 km over two M2 cycles). Rather than patch it, the analysis was reframed as a steady design-current mixing-zone study, matching §316(a) practice."},{"title":"Silent numerical diffusion","text":"First-order upwind added about 2.1 m²/s of numerical diffusion at 25 m resolution, around 20% of the dispersion the model used, with no warning. Against scale-dependent ocean mixing it is larger than the real thing below about 3 km."}],"monitoring":[{"title":"Turbidity masquerading as impact","text":"Detection failure that rose with turbidity looked exactly like animals leaving. Only the detection-corrected occupancy model separated the two."},{"title":"Conditioning, not tolerance","text":"At long range in turbid water, transmittance fell to about 5×10⁻⁸, amplifying rounding error about 20 million-fold in the image round-trip test. The loosened tolerance was replaced with a conditioning table that flags unrecoverable frames."}],"aquaculture":[{"title":"205 tracks for 12 fish","text":"The tracker fell apart because of camera siting: fish moved 34 pixels per frame across a 37 cm field of view. Correcting the geometry and arena size brought track purity to 0.998, 0.935 and 0.678 for calm, moderate and erratic schools."},{"title":"A hypothesis that didn't survive","text":"Kalman-filtered velocities were expected to recover school polarisation better than raw frame differencing. The sweep showed filtering only wins when localisation noise is large relative to per-frame motion. The notebook reports the trade-off instead of the original claim."},{"title":"Yield optimum below growth optimum","text":"Because the oxygen- and ammonia-limited stocking ceiling falls as water warms, the economically best loop temperature is cooler than the temperature at which fish grow fastest."}],"purity":[{"school":"Calm","purity":0.998},{"school":"Moderate","purity":0.935},{"school":"Erratic","purity":0.678}]}}